$\textbf{(A) } \$14.20 \qquad \textbf{(B) } \$16.75 \qquad \textbf{(C) } \$17.75 \qquad \textbf{(D) } \$18.75 \qquad \textbf{(E) } \$19.25$
$\textbf{Solution:}$ We find the cost of each fruit and add them up. Bananas cost $4 \times 1.20 = \$4.80$. Apples cost $3 \times 3 = \$9$. Strawberries cost $24 \times 0.75 = \$18$. Avocados cost $2 \times 2 = \$4$. Grapes cost $10 \times 0.50 = \$5$. Adding these together, the fruit basket costs $4.80 + 9 + 18 + 4 + 5 = \$36$. \boxed{\textbf{(E) } \$19.25}
